From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean O'Hollaren <sean.ohollaren@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:41:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FM-1: a filter over the game's sound on KNOB 1 (sweep) and
 KNOB 2 (resonance), EDIT turns it off

fm1_filter.h is a trapezoidal state-variable filter in fixed point: left of centre a low-pass
closing from 8 kHz to 80 Hz, right of centre a high-pass opening the same way, the centre off
(samples untouched). Settings are ramped across a block and off/on is a crossfade. fm1_controls.c
owns the two settings and says them on the message line; the browser build runs the filter in
its audio callback, the device in its audio interrupt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fm1/fm1.h          |   3 +
 src/fm1/fm1_controls.c |  26 +++++++++
 src/fm1/fm1_filter.h   | 130 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/fm1/fm1_web.c      |   3 +
 4 files changed, 162 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/fm1/fm1_filter.h

